// Horror from the Deep - main quest dialogue and puzzles
// Walkthrough (re-verified this pass): https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Horror_from_the_Deep
// Requires quest_barcrawl complete (already implemented - see ~visited_all_bars).
// Uses ~chatplayer/~chatnpc rather than ~mesbox's @tag@ speaker shorthand, since that shorthand
// depends on a per-NPC abbreviation registered elsewhere that I haven't located/verified for
// Larrissa/Jossik/Gunnjorn - safer to stick to the plain, confirmed primitives.
//
// Item/NPC/loc tags below were cross-checked against the real 377 cache dump
// (content/scripts/_unpack/377/all.{obj,npc,loc}) rather than guessed - the quest's actual assets
// are already present there (this cache already shipped this content in 2006), which is a much
// stronger source than my memory of the wiki walkthrough. Notable corrections made this pass:
//   - horror_lighthouse_key -> horror_key, horror_rusty_casket -> horror_casket (my invented names
//     were wrong - the real tags were sitting right there in all.obj)
//   - damaged prayer books are unfinished_saradominbook / unfinished_zamorakbook / unfinished_guthixbook
//   - bridge item is `woodplank` (all.obj name=Plank), not `plank`; nails item is `nails`
//     (all.obj name=Steel nails) - confirmed via the wiki that repair needs a hammer + 60 nails + 2
//     planks total, split across the two broken spans (horror_broken_bridge_left_spot /
//     _right_spot - both real loc tags, replacing my earlier guessed horror_broken_bridge1/2)
// All quest loc/NPC world placements below are now confirmed, cross-checked two ways: against
// content/maps/*.jm2 (id-based placement data, content/pack/{loc,npc}.pack for id<->name) and,
// for Larrissa, independently in-game via Corey's own ::getcoord (matched exactly). An earlier pass
// this session reported zero placements for several of these - that was wrong on two counts, both
// fixed: (1) a grep `$`-anchor bug against this file format's CRLF line endings silently ate real
// matches, and (2) horror_lighthouse_doorway's id was misread as 4578 (that's the .pack file's own
// line number) when the real id is 4577 (4578 is a different loc, horror_lighthouse_inactive).
//   - horror_lighthouse_windpower_cog (loc 4590, the lighting mechanism): m39_56.jm2, plane 2,
//     local(11,50) = world(2507,3634,2). horror_lighthouse_cog_broken (loc 4588, the original wrong
//     guess) is confirmed genuinely unplaced anywhere searched.
//   - horror_lighthouse_doorway (loc 4577): m39_56.jm2, plane 0, local(13,52) = world(2509,3636,0) -
//     Corey confirmed in-game this is the lighthouse's plain building entrance (real cache def:
//     op1=Walk-through), NOT the six-icon rune/sword/arrow puzzle door I'd guessed it was - that
//     puzzle's real loc is still unknown, see the comment above its (now commented-out) handler below.
//   - horror_ladder_top (loc 4383, real op1=Climb) / horror_ladder_down (loc 4380, no op, decorative):
//     m39_56.jm2, plane 0, local(13,60)/local(12,60) = world(2509,3644,0)/world(2508,3644,0) - the way
//     down to the basement, per Corey's in-game find ("iron ladder to basement"). No script exists for
//     the Climb op yet since there's no known destination - this is now the concrete blocker.
//   - horror_girlfriend_prequest / Larrissa (npc 1336): m39_56.jm2, plane 0, local(12,51) =
//     world(2508,3635,0) - matches Corey's in-game ::getcoord reading exactly.
//   - horror_lighthousekeeeper_well / Jossik (npc 1334): m39_56.jm2, plane 1, local(13,55) =
//     world(2509,3639,1). Only this variant is placed, not horror_lighthousekeeeper_injured (1335) -
//     see the merged opnpc1 handler below for how that's handled.
//   - gunnjorn (npc 607): m39_55.jm2, plane 0, local(44,28) = world(2540,3548,0) - near the real
//     Barbarian Outpost agility arena, matching his own dialogue.
// horror_girlfriend_postquest (1337) is still genuinely unplaced - see its handler below.
//
// UPDATE (2026-09-03): Corey supplied real in-game coords for the lighthouse basement this pass,
// resolving what used to be this quest's one real remaining blocker. horror_lighthousekeeeper_
// injured (1335, "Fallen Jossik") IS genuinely placed after all - m39_72.jm2, plane 0, local(22,25),
// matching Corey's coord exactly - so the merged well/injured handler below is now split back into
// two (see the "Fallen Jossik" section). The strange wall puzzle's real locs were also found in the
// same region (horror_mid_left_door/_mid_right_door, op1=Study; horror_far_right_door/_far_left_door,
// op1=Open - all four tagged "Strange wall", m39_72 plane 1, local z=19 x=17-20) and the six-icon rune/
// sword/arrow logic below is re-attached to them (wiki-reconfirmed this pass, see that section).
// horror_ladder_top's Climb op (previously unscripted - "no known destination") now goes to
// horror_ladder_base2 in that same region, resolving the basement connector too.
//
// Still open: the quest's own boss encounters. m39_156.jm2 - a different region, but with byte-
// identical loc layout to m39_72 (same puzzle room shape, no locs of its own) - turned up placements
// for horror_dagganoth_jr/_jr_darker/_jr_lighter and horror_dagannoth_medium/_darker/_lighter (npcs
// 1338-1343), which is the "level 100 Dagannoth" encounter chamber referenced in Jossik's own
// dialogue below.
//
// RESOLVED (2026-09-08): horror_ladder_base (loc 4412, m39_72 plane 1 local(23,10), real op1=Climb)
// is the connector, and it now has a handler. It was the one isolated, unpaired ladder left in the
// room, and wiring it makes every other loose end in this cave fit together at once - the two
// declared-but-unused constants ^horror_ladder_door_room_dest and ^horror_ladder_dag_dest both land
// exactly where they need to, and the loop Jossik's chamber -> wall room -> p1 cavern -> dagannoth
// cavern -> back closes with no orphans left over. See quest_horror.constant for the full topology.
// Dagannoth Mother has no world placement because she is a scripted spawn, like the level-100
// Dagannoth: both are added on arrival in the cavern (see ~horror_dag_cavern_arrive below).

[opnpc1,horror_girlfriend_prequest]
if (%horror = ^horror_not_started) {
    ~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Hello, is everything alright?");
    ~chatnpc("<p,sad>Oh, adventurer, thank goodness! Something dreadful has happened - the lighthouse has stopped working, and I fear something has happened to Jossik, the lighthouse keeper!");
    ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>The lighthouse guards the coast, doesn't it? Someone should find out what's wrong.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,sad>Would you? Please, I'm too afraid to go in there myself. My name is Larrissa.");
    def_int $op = ~p_choice2("I'll take a look.", 1, "Sorry, I'm busy right now.", 2);
    if ($op = 2) {
        ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Sorry, I'm busy right now.");
        return;
    }
    ~chatplayer("<p,happy>I'll take a look.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,happy>Oh, thank you! The bridges to the east are broken though - you'll need some planks to cross them. My cousin Gunnjorn, at the Barbarian Outpost agility arena, might be able to help you further.");
    %horror = ^horror_started;
    ~send_quest_progress(questlist:horror, 1, ^horror_complete);
} else if (%horror = ^horror_started & getbit_range(%horror_wall, 0, 5) < 63) {
    ~chatnpc("<p,worried>Have you found a way into the lighthouse yet?");
    ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Not yet - I think I need to get it working again first.");
} else if (%horror >= ^horror_started & %horror < ^horror_complete) {
    ~chatnpc("<p,worried>Please be careful down there.");
} else {
    ~chatnpc("<p,happy>Thank you again for rescuing Jossik!");
}

// Only horror_girlfriend_prequest (npc 1336) is actually placed in the map (confirmed both via
// content/maps/m39_56.jm2, plane 0, local(12,51) = world(2508,3635,0), and independently in-game via
// ::getcoord) - horror_girlfriend_postquest (npc 1337) has zero placements. Harmless unlike Jossik's
// case: the prequest handler's own terminal `else` above already covers %horror >= ^horror_complete
// with correct post-quest dialogue, so this handler is unreachable dead code, kept only in case 1337
// ever gets placed for real.
[opnpc1,horror_girlfriend_postquest]
~chatnpc("<p,happy>Thank you again for rescuing Jossik - I don't know what I'd have done without you.");


// Gunnjorn is reachable at the Barbarian Outpost agility arena independent of the broken bridges,
// so the key hand-out is gated on possession (not a %horror stage) to avoid an order-dependent
// sequence break if he's spoken to before or after the bridges are repaired.
// [opnpc1,gunnjorn] can only be declared once globally - this merges in the original base flavour
// dialogue from area_barbarian_outpost/scripts/gunnjorn.rs2 (now removed from there, see that file's
// own comment) as the not-yet-quest-relevant case, rather than dropping it in favour of the quest line.
[opnpc1,gunnjorn]
if (%horror = ^horror_not_started) {
    ~chatnpc("<p,happy>Haha welcome to my obstacle course.|Have fun, but remember this isn't a child's playground.|People have died here.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,happy>The best way to train,|is to go round the course in a clockwise direction.");
} else if (%horror = ^horror_started & inv_total(inv, horror_key) = 0) {
    ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Larrissa said you might be able to help me get into the lighthouse.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Ah, poor Jossik. Here, take this key - it should let you into the basement once you're inside.");
    inv_add(inv, horror_key, 1);
    ~chatplayer("<p,happy>Thanks, I'll head back and see what I can do.");
} else if (%horror >= ^horror_started) {
    ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Good luck down there.");
}


// --- The Lighthouse's building doorway (loc 4577) ---
// Corey (2026-09-03): this was giving "Nothing interesting happens" - the loc itself was placement-
// confirmed earlier this project (see header comment above) but never actually got a handler written
// for its one real op. Real cache def: op1=Walk-through, desc="Lets you walk through walls!" - not a
// puzzle, not gated on quest state, just a thin decorative wall segment you click through rather than
// path around, the same "op1=Walk-through" mechanic the raw cache also uses for a handful of other
// quests' thin walls/doors (bedabin_tentdoor, magearena_scan, legendsquest_force_barrier,
// freedomfighterundergrounddooropenl/r - none scripted anywhere in this codebase yet, no existing
// precedent to copy, so this follows the established `coord()`/`movecoord()`/`p_teleport()` pattern
// already used by this codebase's own ladder-teleport code (ladders+stairs/scripts/ladders.rs2)
// instead. The doorway sits on the wall row at m39_56 plane 0 local z=52 (loc 4577, local(13,52)) -
// Larrissa stands one tile south of it at local(12,51), confirming the outside/quest-start side is
// z<=52 and the lighthouse interior is z>=53 - so this moves the player 2 tiles across whichever side
// of that wall row they're standing on when they click it, working in both directions.
[oploc1,horror_lighthouse_doorway]
p_arrivedelay;
if (coordz(coord()) <= 52) {
    p_teleport(movecoord(coord(), 0, 0, 2));
} else {
    p_teleport(movecoord(coord(), 0, 0, -2));
}


// --- Bridges east of the Lighthouse ---
// One broken crossing, two "Broken bridge" locs (horror_broken_bridge_left_spot /
// _right_spot) with the impassable gap tile between them - see the geometry note under the Cross
// handlers below.
//
// FIXED: the two spans used to be repaired independently, left span -> bit 0 and right span -> bit
// 1, which deadlocked the quest. The gap between them is impassable, so a player on the west shore
// can only ever reach the west span and a player on the east shore only the east one: nobody could
// ever set both bits, and the crossing needs both. Repair is now span-agnostic - either loc accepts
// planks and fills the next empty bit - so the same two planks and 60 nails still repair the whole
// bridge, from whichever side you happen to be standing on.
// Wiki: "use a hammer and 60 steel nails with 2 planks to cross the broken bridge" - 30 nails and
// 1 plank per application. Hammer is a tool (checked, not consumed).
[oplocu,horror_broken_bridge_left_spot]
@horror_repair_bridge;

[oplocu,horror_broken_bridge_right_spot]
@horror_repair_bridge;

[label,horror_repair_bridge]
if (last_useitem ! woodplank) {
    ~displaymessage(^dm_default);
    return;
}
if (%horror < ^horror_started) {
    mes("You should speak to Larrissa first.");
    return;
}
if (getbit_range(%horror_bridges, 0, 1) = 3) {
    mes("This bridge has already been repaired.");
    return;
}
if (inv_total(inv, hammer) = 0) {
    mes("You'll need a hammer to secure the plank in place.");
    return;
}
if (inv_total(inv, nails) < 30) {
    mes("You don't have enough nails to secure the plank - you'll need at least 30.");
    return;
}
inv_del(inv, woodplank, 1);
inv_del(inv, nails, 30);
def_int $bit = 0;
if (testbit(%horror_bridges, 0) = 1) {
    $bit = 1;
}
%horror_bridges = setbit(%horror_bridges, $bit);
if (getbit_range(%horror_bridges, 0, 1) = 3) {
    mes("You nail the last plank into place. The bridge is whole again.");
    return;
}
mes("You nail a plank across the broken span. It'll take another to finish the job.");


// The two spans also carry a real op1=Cross that nothing was wired to, so once you'd repaired the
// bridge there was still no way over it. Geometry read straight out of content/maps/m40_56.jm2
// (plane 1, z=24): viking_pier3_hillskew x=35, horror_broken_bridge_left_spot x=36, the decorative
// horror_broken_bridge x=37, horror_broken_bridge_right_spot x=38, viking_pier3_hillskew x=39.
// The MAP section gives those tiles land flags f2/f3 - f2 is GameMap.LINK_BELOW ("bridge"), so the
// engine registers this whole row at level 0 (GameMap.ts:229-230/263-264), which is why every coord
// below is written 0_40_56_*. x=37 carries f3 = LINK_BELOW|blocked: that is the gap, and it is the
// only reason the crossing needs a script at all - both spans are blockwalk=no, so the player walks
// onto them freely and only the one tile between them is impassable.
// World coords: west span (2596,3608), gap (2597,3608), east span (2598,3608).
//
// [oploc1] only, unlike the basalt rocks in horror_basalt.rs2, which needed [aploc1] because no
// tile beside them is ever walkable. Both spans here ARE walkable (blockwalk=no, and the pier runs
// right up to each of them), so the engine can path the player onto whichever span is on their own
// side and fire the op normally. Clicking the far span across the gap correctly says "I can't reach
// that" - adding an ap trigger would only make that click silently do nothing from 10 tiles away,
// since ap fires and ends the interaction before the player ever walks into range.
[oploc1,horror_broken_bridge_left_spot]  ~horror_cross_bridge;
[oploc1,horror_broken_bridge_right_spot] ~horror_cross_bridge;

[proc,horror_cross_bridge]
if (%horror < ^horror_started) {
    mes("You should speak to Larrissa first.");
    return;
}
if (getbit_range(%horror_bridges, 0, 1) ! 3) {
    mes("The bridge is still broken - both spans need new planks before anyone can cross.");
    return;
}
def_coord $start = 0_40_56_36_24;
def_coord $end = 0_40_56_38_24;
def_int $dir = ^exact_east;
if (coordx(coord) > 2597) {
    $start = 0_40_56_38_24;
    $end = 0_40_56_36_24;
    $dir = ^exact_west;
}
def_int $dist = add(~abs_value(sub(coordx(coord), coordx($start))), ~abs_value(sub(coordz(coord), coordz($start))));
if ($dist > 4) {
    mes("You need to be closer to the bridge to cross it.");
    return;
}
if ($dist > 0) {
    p_walk($start);
    p_delay($dist);
}
mes("You cross the repaired bridge.");
sound_synth(jump_no_land, 1, 20);
~agility_exactmove(human_steppingstonejump, 20, 2, $start, $end, 48, 60, $dir, false);
p_teleport($end);
p_delay(1);

// --- Lighting the lighthouse (roof) ---
// %horror_lighting bits: 0 = swamp tar used, 1 = tinderbox used, 2 = molten glass used
[oplocu,horror_lighthouse_windpower_cog]
if (%horror < ^horror_started) {
    mes("You should investigate the lighthouse first.");
    return;
}
if (getbit_range(%horror_lighting, 0, 2) = 7) {
    mes("The lighting mechanism is already lit.");
    return;
}
if (last_useitem = swamp_tar) {
    if (testbit(%horror_lighting, 0) = 1) {
        mes("You've already applied the swamp tar.");
        return;
    }
    inv_del(inv, swamp_tar, 1);
    mes("You smear the swamp tar over the mechanism.");
    %horror_lighting = setbit(%horror_lighting, 0);
} else if (last_useitem = tinderbox) {
    if (testbit(%horror_lighting, 1) = 1) {
        mes("You've already struck the tinderbox here.");
        return;
    }
    mes("You strike the tinderbox against the mechanism.");
    %horror_lighting = setbit(%horror_lighting, 1);
} else if (last_useitem = molten_glass) {
    if (testbit(%horror_lighting, 2) = 1) {
        mes("You've already fitted the glass.");
        return;
    }
    inv_del(inv, molten_glass, 1);
    mes("You fit the molten glass into the housing.");
    %horror_lighting = setbit(%horror_lighting, 2);
} else {
    ~displaymessage(^dm_default);
    return;
}
if (getbit_range(%horror_lighting, 0, 2) = 7) {
    mes("With a satisfying click, the lighthouse's lamp roars back to life!");
}


// --- The strange wall (basement, m39_72) - RE-ATTACHED (2026-09-03) ---
// Real locs confirmed via content/maps/m39_72.jm2 (all four sit in one row, plane 1, local z=19,
// x=17-20): horror_mid_left_door/horror_mid_right_door (loc 4543/4544, name="Strange wall", real
// op1=Study) and horror_far_right_door/horror_far_left_door (loc 4545/4546, name="Strange wall",
// real op1=Open, desc "appears to be hinged" - these two are the actual hinged doors; the mid pair
// are just the engraved wall panels you study/use items on). Puzzle mechanic wiki-reconfirmed this
// pass (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Horror_from_the_Deep): use one of each elemental rune
// (fire/air/water/earth), a sword, and an arrow, each consumed once regardless of stack size, in any
// order - "you do not get these back" per the wiki, which corrects the original draft of this logic
// (kept below, now fixed) that only deleted the runes and not the sword/arrow. The four physical
// panels aren't distinguished by the wiki, so all four accept any of the six items against one
// shared %horror_wall bitfield (bits: 0=fire, 1=air, 2=water, 3=earth, 4=sword, 5=arrow).
[oplocu,horror_mid_left_door]
@horror_wall_useitem;

[oplocu,horror_mid_right_door]
@horror_wall_useitem;

[oplocu,horror_far_right_door]
@horror_wall_useitem;

[oplocu,horror_far_left_door]
@horror_wall_useitem;

[label,horror_wall_useitem]
if (%horror < ^horror_started) {
    mes("You should investigate the lighthouse first.");
    return;
}
if (getbit_range(%horror_wall, 0, 5) = 63) {
    mes("The wall has already been opened.");
    return;
}
def_int $bit = -1;
if (last_useitem = firerune) {
    $bit = 0;
} else if (last_useitem = airrune) {
    $bit = 1;
} else if (last_useitem = waterrune) {
    $bit = 2;
} else if (last_useitem = earthrune) {
    $bit = 3;
} else if (last_useitem = bronze_sword | last_useitem = iron_sword | last_useitem = steel_sword | last_useitem = black_sword | last_useitem = mithril_sword | last_useitem = adamant_sword | last_useitem = rune_sword) {
    $bit = 4;
} else if (last_useitem = bronze_arrow | last_useitem = iron_arrow | last_useitem = steel_arrow | last_useitem = mithril_arrow | last_useitem = adamant_arrow | last_useitem = rune_arrow) {
    $bit = 5;
} else {
    ~displaymessage(^dm_default);
    return;
}
if (testbit(%horror_wall, $bit) = 1) {
    mes("You've already pressed something like that into the wall.");
    return;
}
mes("You press the item into a hidden recess in the wall.");
%horror_wall = setbit(%horror_wall, $bit);
inv_del(inv, last_useitem, 1);
if (getbit_range(%horror_wall, 0, 5) = 63) {
    mes("With a grinding of stone, the two hinged panels swing back, opening the way south.");
    ~horror_wall_open_doors;
    if (%horror < ^horror_wall_opened) {
        %horror = ^horror_wall_opened;
        ~send_quest_progress(questlist:horror, 2, ^horror_complete);
    }
}

[oploc1,horror_mid_left_door]
gosub(horror_wall_study);

[oploc1,horror_mid_right_door]
gosub(horror_wall_study);

[proc,horror_wall_study]
if (getbit_range(%horror_wall, 0, 5) = 63) {
    mes("The wall has already been opened.");
    return;
}
mes("A strange wall, engraved with symbols representing fire, air, water, earth, a sword and an arrow. There seem to be hidden recesses matching each symbol.");

[oploc1,horror_far_right_door]
gosub(horror_wall_open_attempt);

[oploc1,horror_far_left_door]
gosub(horror_wall_open_attempt);

[proc,horror_wall_open_attempt]
if (getbit_range(%horror_wall, 0, 5) ! 63) {
    mes("The door won't budge - it looks like it's sealed shut somehow.");
    return;
}
mes("You push the hinged panel aside.");
~horror_wall_open_doors;

// FIXED (2026-09-08): the wall never actually opened. The old code did
//     loc_change(horror_far_left_door_inactive, ...); loc_change(horror_far_right_door_inactive, ...);
// which has two separate bugs. First, loc_change acts on the ACTIVE loc, so both calls landed on the
// one panel the player had just clicked - the second simply overwrote the first and the other panel
// was never touched. Second, and fatally, neither _inactive type declares blockwalk=no, and
// LocType.blockwalk defaults to true (engine/src/cache/config/LocType.ts:79) - so even the panel that
// did change stayed exactly as solid as before, just no longer clickable. The six-icon puzzle could
// be solved and the passage south still could not be walked through: a hard quest block.
//
// Both panels are now looked up by their own coordinates and deleted outright, which is the only
// thing that reliably drops a wall loc's collision. ^horror_wall_reopen_delay is short so the wall
// closes behind the player - a player who has already solved it re-opens it any time via Open above,
// and one who hasn't still has to place all six items.
[proc,horror_wall_open_doors]
if (loc_find(^horror_far_left_door_coord, horror_far_left_door) = true) {
    loc_del(^horror_wall_reopen_delay);
}
if (loc_find(^horror_far_right_door_coord, horror_far_right_door) = true) {
    loc_del(^horror_wall_reopen_delay);
}


// --- Lighthouse bookcase (horror_bookcase, loc 4617, real op1=Search) ---
// Placed at m39_56 plane 1 local(12,60) - the lighthouse's middle floor - and again in the m38_71
// copy of that room. The Search option had no handler at all, so it did nothing. There's no item
// reward attached to it in the cache, so it's wired as the puzzle's in-world hint instead: the
// strange wall's six recesses are otherwise only described by studying the wall itself, which you
// can't do until you're already past it.
[oploc1,horror_bookcase]
mes("You search the shelves.");
p_delay(1);
if (%horror < ^horror_started) {
    ~mesbox("Shipping manifests, tide tables and a keeper's journal. The last few entries are about noises from under the lighthouse.");
    return;
}
if (getbit_range(%horror_wall, 0, 5) = 63) {
    ~mesbox("Shipping manifests and tide tables. Nothing else in here seems useful now.");
    return;
}
~mesbox("Tucked among the tide tables is a keeper's journal. One page describes a sealed door beneath the lighthouse, and copies out a rhyme carved beside it:");
~mesbox("'Fire and air, water and earth, a blade and a shaft - press each to its own mark, and the way shall open.'");

// --- The lighthouse's basement ladder (m39_56 <-> m39_72) - RESOLVED (2026-09-03) ---
// horror_ladder_top (loc 4383, real op1=Climb, m39_56) previously had no script since there was no
// known destination - Corey's coords this pass confirmed it. Lands at horror_ladder_base2 (loc 4413,
// real op1=Climb, m39_72 plane 0 local(19,23)), the small chamber Jossik himself sits in
// (local(22,25), a few tiles over - matches the wiki's "Jossik sitting injured by the ladder").
[oploc1,horror_ladder_top]
mes("You climb down the ladder into darkness.");
p_telejump(^horror_ladder_cave_dest);

// horror_ladder_base2 (loc 4413, m39_72 plane 0 local(19,23)) and horror_ladder_top2 (loc 4485, real
// op1=Climb, m39_72 plane 1 local(19,22)) sit right on top of each other, adjacent tile/adjacent
// plane - both are "climb up" triggers out of Jossik's chamber up to the strange-wall floor above it
// (two ladder objects in the same small space - redundant but not a bug, same as a couple of other
// spots this project has found duplicate functional locs). Corey corrected horror_ladder_top2's
// destination directly (2026-09-03, round 5: "the id for the ladder is 4485 ... it takes you
// 1,39,72,19,21") - landing one tile off the loc's own dump tile (19,22), the same "destination tile
// is adjacent to the loc's own placement, not on top of it" pattern already seen elsewhere. No loc
// was found leading back down to Jossik's chamber from up here, so that return trip is currently a
// gap - flagged in the project doc rather than invented.
[oploc1,horror_ladder_base2]
mes("You climb up the ladder.");
p_telejump(^horror_ladder_wallroom_dest);

// FIXED (2026-09-08): horror_ladder_top2 is the ladder object on the UPPER floor (m39_72 plane 1
// local(19,22), right beside the decorative horror_ladder_join) and it was sending the player UP to
// the wall room they are already standing in - a no-op click, and it left the trip back down to
// Jossik with no route at all, which the old comment above flagged as an open gap. It goes down now,
// to ^horror_ladder_dag_dest (0_39_72_19_24) - a constant that was declared for exactly this and
// never used, one tile north of horror_ladder_base2's own tile in Jossik's chamber.
[oploc1,horror_ladder_top2]
mes("You climb down the ladder.");
p_telejump(^horror_ladder_dag_dest);


// horror_ladder_base (loc 4412, m39_72 plane 1 local(23,10), real op1=Climb) - the unpaired ladder
// in the big cavern south of the strange wall, which had no handler at all. It is the way into the
// dagannoth cavern (m39_156), and the same loc in that region is the way back up to the door room.
[oploc1,horror_ladder_base]
if (coordz(coord) > ^horror_dag_cavern_z_min) {
    mes("You climb back up the ladder.");
    p_telejump(^horror_ladder_door_room_dest);
    return;
}
mes("You climb down into a vast, echoing cavern.");
p_telejump(^horror_dag_cavern_arrival);
~horror_dag_cavern_arrive;

// Both bosses are spawned on arrival rather than placed in the map, and only for a player who still
// needs them - so they are never standing around for someone who has already finished, and a player
// who logged out mid-fight gets them back simply by climbing down again. Guarded so a second player
// arriving during a fight does not stack a duplicate.
[proc,horror_dag_cavern_arrive]
if (%horror = ^horror_wall_opened) {
    if (npc_findexact(^horror_dag_cavern_jr4_spawn, horror_dagannoth_jr4) = false) {
        npc_add(^horror_dag_cavern_jr4_spawn, horror_dagannoth_jr4, ^horror_boss_lifetime);
        mes("Something enormous shifts in the dark ahead of you.");
    }
    return;
}
if (%horror = ^horror_dagannoth_defeated) {
    if (~horror_mother_present = false) {
        ~horror_spawn_mother;
    }
}


// --- Fallen Jossik (found injured, underground) and horror_lighthousekeeeper_well (topside, the
// final reward exchange) - SPLIT (2026-09-03) ---
// horror_lighthousekeeeper_injured (npc 1335, "Fallen Jossik") is genuinely placed after all -
// content/maps/m39_72.jm2, plane 0, local(22,25), matching Corey's own in-game coord exactly. That
// resolves the uncertainty the merged handler below used to carry (no confirmed way to changetype a
// *different* non-combat npc instance from a loc/dialogue context) - there's no changetype needed at
// all, since injured Jossik and well Jossik are just two separate, independently-placed npcs in two
// separate locations: injured underground for the whole time the player's down here with him, well
// topside in the lighthouse (m39_56, plane 1, local(13,55)) once the player's made it back up with
// the casket. Split along that boundary.
// FIXED (2026-09-08): this used to DRIVE the stage machine instead of reacting to it - simply
// meeting Jossik jumped %horror from ^horror_wall_opened straight to ^horror_dagannoth_defeated,
// and nothing anywhere ever set ^horror_mother_defeated. The quest therefore stuck at stage 3
// forever and could not be completed by anyone. Both stages are now set by the kills themselves,
// in quest_horror_combat.rs2, and this handler only reads them.
[opnpc1,horror_lighthousekeeeper_injured]
if (%horror < ^horror_dagannoth_defeated) {
    ~chatplayer("<p,shock>Jossik! Are you alright?");
    ~chatnpc("<p,sad>Adventurer! Thank Guthix... there are creatures down here, dagannoth of some kind.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,worried>There's a strange wall on the floor above us. Whatever has been making the noise, it came from behind it. Please, be careful.");
} else if (%horror < ^horror_mother_defeated) {
    ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>I killed the thing behind the wall.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,worried>That wasn't it. There's something bigger down there... I can hear it moving.");
} else if (%horror < ^horror_casket_given) {
    ~chatplayer("<p,happy>It's dead. I found this rusty casket where it was nesting.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>A casket? Let's get out of here and I'll take a look upstairs.");
    %horror = ^horror_casket_given;
    ~send_quest_progress(questlist:horror, 5, ^horror_complete);
} else {
    ~chatnpc("<p,relieved>Let's get back up top - I don't want to spend any longer down here than I have to.");
}

[opnpc1,horror_lighthousekeeeper_well]
if (%horror >= ^horror_casket_given & %horror < ^horror_complete) {
    ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Here's that casket I found.");
    inv_del(inv, horror_casket, 1);
    ~chatnpc("<p,happy>Ah, I recognise this - it's one of ours. There should be a damaged prayer book inside. Which order would you like?");
    @multi4("A book of Saradomin.", horror_book_saradomin, "A book of Zamorak.", horror_book_zamorak, "A book of Guthix.", horror_book_guthix, "None for me, thanks.", horror_book_none);
} else if (%horror >= ^horror_complete) {
    // Two separate post-quest services, which the old single ~openshop_activenpc call conflated:
    // the wiki's 5,000gp replacement for a LOST damaged prayer book is a dialogue transaction, and
    // is not in [lighthouseshop]'s stock at all - that inv is the general store ("Jossik's Wares":
    // rope, hammer, chisel, tinderbox, containers, Fremennik drinks), which is what op3=Trade and
    // the "supplies" option below open. See configs/quest_horror_jossik.npc for the shop binding
    // that makes ~openshop_activenpc work at all - before it, npc_param(owned_shop) was unset here.
    ~chatnpc("<p,happy>Hello again. The light's burning bright, thanks to you.");
    def_int $service = ~p_choice3("Could I see what you have for sale?", 1, "I've lost my prayer book.", 2, "Just passing through.", 3);
    if ($service = 3) {
        ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Just passing through.");
        return;
    }
    if ($service = 1) {
        ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Could I see what you have for sale?");
        ~openshop_activenpc;
        return;
    }
    ~chatplayer("<p,sad>I've lost my prayer book.");
    if (~horror_carrying_prayer_book = true) {
        ~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Have you now? You seem to have one on you already.");
        return;
    }
    ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Careless. I can salvage you another from the wreck, but it'll cost you 5,000 coins.");
    if (~p_choice2("That's fine, here you go.", 1, "That's too much.", 2) = 2) {
        ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>That's too much.");
        return;
    }
    ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>That's fine, here you go.");
    if (inv_total(inv, coins) < 5000) {
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>You don't have that much on you.");
        return;
    }
    if (inv_freespace(inv) < 1) {
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>You'll need a free hand to carry it.");
        return;
    }
    ~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Which order was yours again?");
    @multi3("A book of Saradomin.", horror_rebuy_saradomin, "A book of Zamorak.", horror_rebuy_zamorak, "A book of Guthix.", horror_rebuy_guthix);
}

// True if the player already has any of the three prayer books, damaged or finished, carried or
// worn - keeps the 5,000gp replacement from handing out a second copy of a book they still have.
[proc,horror_carrying_prayer_book]()(boolean)
if (inv_total(inv, unfinished_saradominbook) > 0 | inv_total(inv, unfinished_zamorakbook) > 0 | inv_total(inv, unfinished_guthixbook) > 0) {
    return(true);
}
if (inv_total(inv, saradominbook_complete) > 0 | inv_total(inv, zamorakbook_complete) > 0 | inv_total(inv, guthixbook_complete) > 0) {
    return(true);
}
if (inv_total(worn, saradominbook_complete) > 0 | inv_total(worn, zamorakbook_complete) > 0 | inv_total(worn, guthixbook_complete) > 0) {
    return(true);
}
return(false);

// The coins come off inside each label rather than before the @multi3 above: ~multi3, like every
// other dialogue primitive, ends in p_pausebutton and is abortable, so charging before the choice
// would take 5,000gp from anyone who closed the window.
[label,horror_rebuy_saradomin]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>A book of Saradomin.");
@horror_rebuy_give(unfinished_saradominbook);

[label,horror_rebuy_zamorak]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>A book of Zamorak.");
@horror_rebuy_give(unfinished_zamorakbook);

[label,horror_rebuy_guthix]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>A book of Guthix.");
@horror_rebuy_give(unfinished_guthixbook);

[label,horror_rebuy_give](namedobj $book)
if (inv_total(inv, coins) < 5000) {
    ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>You don't have that much on you.");
    return;
}
inv_del(inv, coins, 5000);
inv_add(inv, $book, 1);
~mesbox("You hand over 5,000 coins and Jossik fetches you another damaged prayer book.");

[label,horror_book_saradomin]
~chatplayer("<p,happy>A book of Saradomin.");
inv_add(inv, unfinished_saradominbook, 1);
~mesbox("Jossik hands you a damaged book of Saradomin, salvaged from the wreck of the casket.");
@finish_horror_quest;

[label,horror_book_zamorak]
~chatplayer("<p,happy>A book of Zamorak.");
inv_add(inv, unfinished_zamorakbook, 1);
~mesbox("Jossik hands you a damaged book of Zamorak, salvaged from the wreck of the casket.");
@finish_horror_quest;

[label,horror_book_guthix]
~chatplayer("<p,happy>A book of Guthix.");
inv_add(inv, unfinished_guthixbook, 1);
~mesbox("Jossik hands you a damaged book of Guthix, salvaged from the wreck of the casket.");
@finish_horror_quest;

[label,horror_book_none]
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>None for me, thanks.");
~chatnpc("<p,happy>Suit yourself - I'll keep hold of it in case you change your mind.");
@finish_horror_quest;

[label,finish_horror_quest]
~chatnpc("<p,happy>Thank you again for everything, adventurer. I don't know what would have happened to me down there without you.");
stat_advance(magic, 46625);
stat_advance(strength, 46625);
stat_advance(ranged, 46625);
mes("Congratulations, you've completed Horror from the Deep!");
%horror = ^horror_complete;
~send_quest_progress(questlist:horror, 6, ^horror_complete);
